Template: led-ugreen-systemd/configure-services
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Configure UGREEN LED services automatically?
 Configure network monitoring and optionally enable services at boot.
 Disk mapping and LED appearance remain in /etc/ugreen-leds.conf.

Template: led-ugreen-systemd/network-mode
Type: select
Choices: single, multi, all
Default: all
Description: Network interface monitoring mode:
 Select one interface, selected interfaces, or all physical Ethernet devices.
 Traffic from every selected interface contributes to the network LED.

Template: led-ugreen-systemd/network-interface
Type: string
Description: Network interfaces to monitor:
 Enter one interface for single mode, or space-separated interfaces for multi
 mode (for example, enp2s0 enp3s0). Leave blank to detect physical interfaces.

Template: led-ugreen-systemd/enable-services
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Enable and start UGREEN LED services?
 Enable services at boot and start them now if systemd is running.
